course: dictionary
lesson: 2782
title: Dishonest
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dishonest means not honest. A dishonest person lies, cheats, steals or tricks people. It is an adjective, so it describes a person, a behaviour or a choice, as in dishonest behaviour.
explain: Look at the context. «Changing a mark or forging a parent's signature is dishonest.» Forging a signature means writing someone's name yourself and pretending they wrote it. That is a trick, so it is dishonest. Check by swapping in your meaning: "Changing a mark is not honest" still makes sense.
explain: Dishonesty hurts trust. «Swapping price stickers is stealing.» If people cannot trust what a shop tells them, they stop coming back. Honest shops last because buyers come back, and the same is true of friends and families.
fact: Dishonest means not honest: lying, cheating, stealing or tricking people.
fact: Useful phrases: a dishonest person, dishonest behaviour, it is dishonest to.
fact: «Claiming feelings just to seem friendly would be dishonest.» Pretending is a form of dishonesty.
fact: In stories, dishonest characters are often found out.
fact: When dishonesty is found out, the trouble is usually much bigger than the first lie or trick.
exercise: Which word means not honest: lying, cheating, stealing or tricking people? | Generous | Honest | *Dishonest | Curious
exercise: «Changing a mark or forging a parent's signature is dishonest.» What is forging a signature? | *Writing a parent's name yourself and pretending they wrote it | Losing your homework book | Drawing a picture of your parent | Asking a parent to sign your book
exercise: A pupil copies a friend's answers and says they did the test alone. Is this dishonest? | Only if the teacher sees it | No, it is a clever shortcut | *Yes, it is dishonest to pretend | It is just a game
test:
«Claiming feelings just to seem friendly would be dishonest.» Why? | *Because it pretends something that is not true | Because friendly words are always rude | Because it is too short | Because friends never talk
Why do honest shops last? | *Buyers trust them and come back | They are always the biggest shops | They never sell anything | They always have the lowest prices
exam: Which sentence uses dishonest correctly? | Dishonest is a colour of the sky. | We ate a dishonest lunch at school. | *It is dishonest to swap the price stickers. | The dishonest sun shone brightly on the hill.
